  "summary": "Skills collection with benign tool and endpoint references",
  "details": "Package ships a collection of 'skills' (helper scripts and documentation) under skills/*. Static pattern matches fire on routine content: skills/rclone-cli/scripts/install.sh fetches rclone from its official project domain (rclone.org) as part of a documented tool install; skills/youtube-notetaker/scripts/verify.sh runs curl/GET verification commands; skills/junta-leiloeiros/scripts/*.py contain ping/GET/POST keywords in Python scraper and local API-serve code; skills/loki-mode/benchmarks/run-benchmarks.sh contains an \"install\" keyword co-occurrence. The matched excerpts show keyword co-occurrence (curl/ping/GET/POST/install) rather than a traced data-exfiltration path: no reads of installer secrets (~/.aws, ~/.ssh, ~/.npmrc, environment scraping), no hardcoded attacker-controlled destination, no install-time lifecycle hook that auto-executes these scripts on npm install, and no obfuscated fetch-and-exec. The referenced external host (rclone.org) is the official project domain for the rclone tool the script is intended to install.",
